+- D-02 (owner revision 2, OWNER_CHANGE.md): Runtime failures retain successful rows and expose individual failed rows. This supersedes the revision-1 API atomic rollback rule and resolves the prior PRODUCT/API disagreement.
+- D-03 (owner revision 2): Every snapshot has contractVersion: 2 and items with original string rowId, status, integer attempts and nullable error, plus batchId/status/total/succeeded/failed. This supersedes aggregate-only snapshots. Attempts count processor calls; failed errors persist through requeue until successful processing.
+- D-04 (owner revision 2): Retry failed rows in the same batch using durable batch-scoped request identities. Replay does not enqueue twice, even after reopen or another failure. A distinct identity may retry recurring failure. Successful records and attempts remain unchanged; successful batch retry is a no-op. Concurrent retry/worker activity must not duplicate attempts or records. This supersedes revision 1's retry exclusion.
+- D-05 (owner revision 2): UI exposes actual asynchronous state and every item outcome, restores active batch on refresh and retains an uncertain retry identity after response loss. Form values survive request failure.
